<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shahrokh Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1796">1796</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shahrokh Shah was a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> who reigned as a nominal Afsharid ruler in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mashhad">Mashhad</a> after being blinded. He survived until 1796, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agha-mohammad-khan-qajar">Agha Mohammad Khan Qajar</a> took the city and had him tortured to death. His death marked the final end of the Afsharid line.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shahrokh-shah.jpg" alt="Shahrokh Shah" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christies.com · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nader_Shah_Afshar_and_his_court,_India_or_Iran,_18th_century_(cropped_2)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
